        "id": 5195,
        "name": "Koga",
        "username": "Koga",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/koga/{size}/2058_2.png",
        "created_at": "2011-09-16T03:42:07.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Got questions about a few cards, some from other people I play with.</p>\n<p><span class=\"bbcode-u\">My own question</span><br>\n<span class=\"bbcode-b\">Smoke Bombs:</span> \"<span class=\"bbcode-i\">Whenever a villain card would damage the hero target with the lowest hp, redirect that damage to the hero target with the highest hp. Reduce damage redirected this way by 1.\"</span><br>\nDoes this card activate whenever the hero with lowest hp gets dealt damage or only if the card specifically targets the hero with the lowest hp? Ex: A card deals damage to each hero, since you can choose the order of how damage is dealt will that activate smoke bombs when it hits the hero with lowest hp? If it does then it makes choosing the order of damage very important but also confusing and could, if the hp was just right, redirect each it.</p>\n<p><span class=\"bbcode-u\">Questions from other players</span><br>\n<span class=\"bbcode-b\">Gene-Bound Banshee:</span> <span class=\"bbcode-i\">At the end of the villain turn, this card deals the hero with the most ongoing cards 3 sonic damage.</span><br>\nIf nobody has any ongoing cards does this card still deal damage or do we just decide who takes the damage?</p>\n<p><span class=\"bbcode-b\">Citizen Summer:</span> <span class=\"bbcode-i\">At the end of the villain turn, this card deals the two heroes with the most cards in play 3 fire damage each.</span><br>\nSimilar to previous card, does this deal damage if no heroes have any cards in play or do we just choose 2 to take the damage?</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:34:46.870Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 1,
        "reads": 0,
        "readers_count": 0,
        "score": 5.0,
